      "scenes": [
        {
          "id": "scene-01",
          "phrases": [
            {
              "id": "s01-p01",
              "text": "At the rear door of the cardiac gallery,",
              "targetId": "rear-door"
            },
            {
              "id": "s01-p02",
              "text": "picture a curved circumflex key.",
              "targetId": "circumflex-key"
            },
            {
              "id": "s01-p03",
              "text": "Keep that same doorway as your memory location whenever coronary dominance returns.",
              "targetId": "rear-door"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "scene-02",
          "phrases": [
            {
              "id": "s02-p01",
              "text": "Coronary dominance follows the artery that gives rise to the posterior descending artery.",
              "targetId": "clinical-pda"
            },
            {
              "id": "s02-p02",
              "text": "On the angiogram, trace that vessel",
              "targetId": "clinical-pda"
            },
            {
              "id": "s02-p03",
              "text": "back to its parent artery.",
              "targetId": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "scene-03",
          "phrases": [
            {
              "id": "s03-p01",
              "text": "In a left-dominant circulation, the posterior descending artery comes from the circumflex.",
              "targetId": "circumflex-key"
            },
            {
              "id": "s03-p02",
              "text": "Its septal branches supply the posterior part of the interventricular septum.",
              "targetId": "posterior-bridge"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "scene-04",
          "phrases": [
            {
              "id": "s04-p01",
              "text": "The circumflex also supplies the lateral left ventricular wall through its branches.",
              "targetId": "lateral-wall"
            },
            {
              "id": "s04-p02",
              "text": "A clot at its origin can therefore threaten both territories downstream.",
              "targetId": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "scene-05",
          "phrases": [
            {
              "id": "s05-p01",
              "text": "For the book's example, combine the lateral left ventricular wall",
              "targetId": "lateral-wall"
            },
            {
              "id": "s05-p02",
              "text": "with the posterior septum.",
              "targetId": "posterior-bridge"
            },
            {
              "id": "s05-p03",
              "text": "Identifying only one of those regions would leave out part of the pattern.",
              "targetId": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "scene-06",
          "phrases": [
            {
              "id": "s06-p01",
              "text": "Return to the rear door:",
              "targetId": "rear-door"
            },
            {
              "id": "s06-p02",
              "text": "the circumflex key opens",
              "targetId": "circumflex-key"
            },
            {
              "id": "s06-p03",
              "text": "the lateral room",
              "targetId": "lateral-wall"
            },
            {
              "id": "s06-p04",
              "text": "and the back septal room.",
              "targetId": "posterior-bridge"
            },
            {
              "id": "s06-p05",
              "text": "The recall cue is simple: left dominance, circumflex supplies the back.",
              "targetId": "posterior-bridge"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "outroTargetId": "clinical-pda",
      "annotationNotes": [
        "The mnemonic bridge is the agreed symbolic mapping for posterior septal territory; it is not anatomy.",
        "The clinical PDA point is on the vessel immediately above the published red arrows in panel (b). The parent-artery phrase deliberately has no pointer: the downloaded source identifies the PDA but does not label an exact parent-vessel point.",
        "Clot, vessel occlusion, and combined supply patterns are not literally drawn; the corresponding abstract phrase has no pointer."
      ]
    },
